The first thing any program in this project does is read this directory.

Right now there is nothing to configure, because nothing has been built. When
there is, this is where a match's opening decisions live: the seed the dunes are
raised from, the size of the field, how many players and which of them are bots,
which catalogue tables to load, and which transport to reach other players over.

The reason this is a directory of files rather than a wall of command-line flags:
a match is a small number of decisions made before it starts, and they should be
readable, diffable, and copyable. A replay header is nearly the same set of
fields. Anything you would want to pin down and hand to somebody else so they can
run the same match belongs here.

What is here already:
    dependencies      -- what the build needs beyond LuaJIT, and where it comes from
    seed              -- the match seed, one integer or the word `random`

What goes here eventually:
    field             -- the dune field's size and roughness, and where the water sits
    players           -- one line per player: a name, a team, person or bot
    catalogues        -- which unit, cost, timer, and experimental tables to load
    transport         -- how other players are reached: `local`, `udp`, or the
                         handheld's peer table
